---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
List recent runs (the default when `snouty runs` runs with no subcommand).

Each run has its ID, status, creation time, launcher, and test name. For a run
with no test name, the name is the first line of its description.

Columns: RUN ID, STATUS, CREATED, LAUNCHER, RUN. RUN is the test name, or `-`
for a run with no test name and no description. CREATED is the age of the run,
such as `2h ago`. Use --detail for the full description and the creation time,
which is in the local timezone. Add --utc to show it in UTC.

--created-after and --created-before take a date, which is the start of that
day, a time as snouty prints it, such as `2026-10-01 12:00:00`, or an RFC 3339
time. A date or a time without a zone is in the local timezone, or in UTC with
--utc. --created-after includes a run created at that time, and --created-before
does not. So a run's Created time with --created-after selects that run and the
runs after it, and with --created-before the runs before it.

Pass a run's ID to `runs show` for its details, to `runs properties` for its
property results, or to `runs wait` to wait until it is ready or complete.

Examples:
  snouty runs list --status completed --limit 5

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each run prints as one JSON object on
its own line, in the order the server returns them:
  snouty --json runs list | jq -r .run_id

Usage: snouty runs list [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -s, --status <STATUS>
          Filter by status
          
          [possible values: starting, in_progress, completed, cancelled,
          incomplete, unknown]

  -l, --launcher <LAUNCHER>
          Filter by launcher name

      --created-after <CREATED_AFTER>
          Only show runs created at or after this date (e.g. 2026-10-01), time
          (e.g. 2026-10-01 12:00:00) or RFC 3339 time

      --created-before <CREATED_BEFORE>
          Only show runs created before this date (e.g. 2026-11-01), time (e.g.
          2026-11-01 12:00:00) or RFC 3339 time

  -n, --limit <LIMIT>
          Maximum number of runs to display
          
          [default: 10]

  -d, --detail
          Show a detailed key-value block per run, including the full
          description

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --utc
          Show times in UTC instead of the local timezone

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
